scope two stranded laps recovered whole; a peer's pen sweep corrected by one line it missed; a REDS fold and a link repair both withdrawn to peers who landed first
status GREEN -- both witnesses re-run on metal concurrently, roster re-verified after two rebases, paper A/93, card under bound
recommend keep-going -- the question both elder laps left is still the one worth taking, and the instrument for it now stands in the tree: one shared 270-byte table is beautiful while the graph is whole, and Comlink nodes leave. Remove one node, rebuild the table from the identity, and count how many of the 719 entries change. That number is the update cost under churn, it decides whether a shared table is usable at all, and the four shapes will not answer it alike.
